### AUTH SERVICE  ·  /auth
### Where tokens come from. Cookies are set by signup/login and resent
### automatically by the REST Client.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = amr@example.com
@password = password123


### Sign up  →  201  ·  already registered → 400
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amr Nashaat",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### Log in  →  200
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}


### Wrong password  →  400. Vague on purpose: must not reveal whether the
### email exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}


### Refresh  →  200 from the refreshToken cookie (401 without it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh


### Log out  →  204, clears the session and the cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
